//? Title: X-bar, R and S charts for rational subgroups
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Each row contains synthetic diameter measurements from one setup. The first
six rows establish the baseline. Later rows include shifts in the mean and
within-setup spread, and the number of measurements per row can vary.
)

> Fit, monitor and plot

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/subgroup_charts.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>


namespace spc = datamunge::stats;
using datamunge::graphics::RLayout;

void show_signals(const spc::ControlChart& chart) {
    for (const auto& p : chart.points)
        if (p.outside)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |\n",
                       chart.title, p.index, p.value, p.lower, p.upper);
}

int main() {
    const std::vector<std::vector<double>> diameters{
        {9.94, 10.02, 10.08, 9.98}, {9.96, 10.01, 10.07, 9.99},
        {9.97, 10.03, 10.08, 9.94}, {9.95, 9.99, 10.01, 10.05},
        {9.97, 10.07, 10.04}, {9.96, 10.03, 10.06, 10.01, 9.94},
        {9.93, 10.00, 10.04, 10.02}, {10.19, 10.25, 10.21, 10.28},
        {9.75, 10.22, 10.17, 9.88, 10.04}, {9.97, 10.04, 10.07}
    };
    const spc::ControlChartOptions baseline{.baseline_size = 6};
    const auto mean_r = spc::xbar_chart(diameters, baseline);
    const auto range = spc::r_chart(diameters, baseline);
    const auto mean_s = spc::xbar_s_chart(diameters, baseline);
    const auto sd = spc::s_chart(diameters, baseline);

    std::print("| Chart | Setup | Statistic | Lower | Upper |\n"
               "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto* chart : {&mean_r, &range, &mean_s, &sd}) show_signals(*chart);

    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    RLayout::create(2, 2).size(1100, 720).add(mean_r.plot()).add(range.plot())
        .add(mean_s.plot()).add(sd.plot()).save_svg("build/subgroup_charts.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Chart | Setup | Statistic | Lower | Upper |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| X-bar chart (range estimate) | 8 | 10.232 | 9.919 | 10.093 |
| R-chart | 9 | 0.470 | 0.000 | 0.285 |
| X-bar chart (SD estimate) | 8 | 10.232 | 9.922 | 10.091 |
| S-chart | 9 | 0.197 | 0.000 | 0.111 |
\image(figures/subgroup_charts.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The X-bar charts track subgroup location, and the R and S charts track subgroup spread.)
\alttext(Four panels show the two X-bar and companion spread charts. Both location and spread limit violations are visible.)

> Interpret the chart

The X-bar charts use the same grand mean with different estimates of the
within-subgroup scale. Compare setup eight, where the location changes, with
setup nine, where the spread grows. The normal range constants restrict the
range-based pair to subgroups of two through ten. The SD-based pair uses
sample-SD moments and accepts any subgroup size of at least two.

> References

- [NIST Shewhart X-bar, R and S control charts|https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section3/pmc321.htm]
